WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.760
If you've traveled on an airplane before&nbsp;
you might have noticed that the shortest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.440
route to your destination doesn't take&nbsp;
you along a straight line on the map&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:15.080
but rather follows a curved path. This is&nbsp;
an example of what's called a geodesic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.760
a route representing the straightest path on&nbsp;
a surface, and to calculate it you need the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:27.160
aid of certain mathematical tools known&nbsp;
as the Christoffel Symbols. Likewise in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.800
general relativity these same tools allow you to&nbsp;
calculate the inertial routes of objects through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:39.280
space and time. But where do such tools&nbsp;
come from and how can we understand them

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:48.120
intuitively? This is Dialect with&nbsp;
Conceptualizing the Christoffel

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:56.880
Symbols. This is Cartesian bear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.760
he lives in Cartesian land, where lines&nbsp;
are all straights and intersect at right

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:11.280
angles this is polar bear he lives in&nbsp;
polar land where lines are all straight and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:19.600
intersect at right angles. Okay aren't these&nbsp;
two lands exactly the same thing? Well sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.560
but not quite. You see Cartesian&nbsp;
Bear lives in the real world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:32.800
where his grid distances and coordinate angles&nbsp;
match up to actual distances and actual angles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.320
while Polar Bear is living in a matrix,&nbsp;
a false projective world like the map on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:45.560
your airplane screen. What this means is that&nbsp;
when Polar Bear moves in a straight line along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:51.360
his Theta coordinate direction in polar land,&nbsp;
he actually moves along a circle in the real

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:59.000
world. And when Polar Bear moves in a straight&nbsp;
line in the r coordinate direction in polar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.800
land he actually moves radially outwards in&nbsp;
the real world, as if along the spokes of a

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:13.280
wheel. Polar Bear is unaware of all this&nbsp;
because he assumed his coordinates to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:20.440
represent independent dimensions and so to&nbsp;
him Polar Land is perfectly Cartesian. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:28.200
one day Cartesian Bear decides to Red Pill poor&nbsp;
Polar Bear. "Your idea of reality is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:33.520
a map," he tells Polar Bear, a projection&nbsp;
due to the false way you constructed your

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:38.960
coordinates. Now Polar Bear descends into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.200
an existential crisis. How can&nbsp;
he know what's real and what's

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:51.720
not? Before in order to measure distances and&nbsp;
angles in Polar Land he had always relied on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.720 --> 00:03:00.280
his basis vectors ER and E Theta. Across Polar&nbsp;
Land these basis vectors always had unit length&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:06.800
one and everywhere were oriented at right angles&nbsp;
to one another. But since realizing he lives in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:13.200
The Matrix, Polar Bear now knows that the lengths&nbsp;
of these basis vectors don't represent true real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:20.360
world lengths, nor does the right angle between&nbsp;
them necessarily represent a real right angle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:26.560
Moreover, the amounts of distance and the angle&nbsp;
these basis vectors do represent could actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:33.800
change from point to point across Polar Land.&nbsp;
Fortunately for Polar Bear we will provide him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:41.160
with a useful mathematical tool known as the&nbsp;
Metric Tensor. If Polar Land is a map of sorts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:47.400
then this tool is like a bar scale for his&nbsp;
basis vectors. It tells him at every point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:54.800
across Polar Land how much real world distance&nbsp;
his basis vectors represent and what the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:03.840
world angle between them is. In this case the&nbsp;
first component of the metric tensor is one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.760
so this tells polar bear that everywhere&nbsp;
in polar land his ER basis vector correctly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:17.440
represents one unit of real world length. Thus&nbsp;
if polar bear moves one unit of R coordinate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.400
distance in Polar Land, he knows he'll also&nbsp;
have moved one unit of distance in the real

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:31.920
world. The second component r-squared tells&nbsp;
Polar Bear that his Theta basis vector represents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.120
as many units of real world distance as is&nbsp;
equal to whatever R coordinate he is located

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:50.200
at. So if Polar Bear is located at R coordinate 2&nbsp;
and moves one unit of theta coordinate distance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:57.880
he will move two units of distance in the real&nbsp;
world. And if he's located at R coordinate 4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:02.920
and moves one unit of theta coordinate distance,&nbsp;
he will move four units of distance in the real

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:10.440
world. This should make intuitive&nbsp;
sense for polar coordinates because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.000
any change in angle will sweep out a&nbsp;
greater distance farther out from the

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:24.760
origin. Finally the last two components of&nbsp;
the metric tensor are both zero, which tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:31.160
polar bear that the 90° angle between his basis&nbsp;
vectors represents 90 degrees in the real world as

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:43.160
well. So it turns out that Polar Bear's theta&nbsp;
ruler essentially grows in length as he moves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:49.920
radially outwards in the real world. This explains&nbsp;
in part why his coordinate construction of Polar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:57.880
Land was false to begin with; however there is&nbsp;
more to the story, for as Cartesian bear can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:03.480
plainly see, when Polar bear moves along a circle&nbsp;
the direction in which he lays out his rulers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:10.760
also steadily rotates and changes. Polar Bear is&nbsp;
still unaware of this however, because although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:15.880
the metric tensor tells him about the real world&nbsp;
lengths of his basis vectors and the relative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:22.840
angle between them it doesn't explicitly specify&nbsp;
anything about the real world orientation of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:30.360
vectors. But is it still possible for Polar Bear&nbsp;
to deduce such information from the metric tensor

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:41.480
alone? Let's have Polar Bear consider just four&nbsp;
infinitesimal pieces of Polar Land at a certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:49.280
R distance out from the coordinate origin. Each&nbsp;
piece has length DR and height D-Theta. We'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:55.960
help him out by drawing the ER and E-Theta basis&nbsp;
vectors on each piece. Now keep in mind that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.120
basis vectors have a unit length of one,&nbsp;
even though we are drawing them as being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:05.840
on par with the infinitesimal lengths of our&nbsp;
pieces. Now the r coordinates of the pieces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.200
in the first column we'll label as R and the r&nbsp;
coordinates of the pieces in the second column&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:18.440
as r + DR. Similarly the theta coordinates of&nbsp;
the rows we'll label as theta and theta plus d-

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:28.240
theta. Now let's resize these pieces to match&nbsp;
their real world areas using the metric tensor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:34.840
We start by multiply in R lengths everywhere&nbsp;
by one. Obviously this means the DR lengths of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:41.480
all the pieces as well as the lengths of all&nbsp;
the R bases vectors remain the same. Next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:48.120
we multiply D-Theta lengths everywhere by their&nbsp;
R coordinate distance out from the origin. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:54.240
means the D Theta lengths of the pieces in the&nbsp;
first column become r d Theta while the Theta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.240 --> 00:08:01.880
bases vectors are resized to length R. In this&nbsp;
the second column meanwhile the D Theta lengths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:09.400
of the pieces become r + Dr * D-Theta and the&nbsp;
theta basis vector lengths become R plus Dr.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:18.720
Polar Bear now has four properly sized pieces&nbsp;
of Cartesian Land, and so to figure out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:24.520
real world orientation of his basis vectors, all&nbsp;
he needs to do is fit these pieces together like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:32.160
puzzle. Indeed, should he find a general method&nbsp;
for fitting pieces together at any arbitrary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:38.240
coordinate, then this would allow him to fit&nbsp;
together every resized piece of Polar Land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:44.440
so as to reconstruct the whole of Cartesian&nbsp;
Land and be able to determine his geodesics upon

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:51.960
it. But how does he go about this using&nbsp;
just the information of the metric tensor

00:08:51.960 --> 00:09:01.360
alone? Well let's examine each metric component&nbsp;
more deeply to see what it's saying. Now the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:06.560
fact that the first component tells us that our&nbsp;
lengths everywhere are unchanging means there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:13.920
no one-dimensional curvature in the R direction&nbsp;
in Polar Land. In terms of our resized pieces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:21.600
this means we can thus conjoin our two columns&nbsp;
side by side without bending or rotating them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:27.000
Meanwhile the fact that the second component tells&nbsp;
us that the theta lengths do change across Polar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:32.600
Land means we won't be able to preserve&nbsp;
the straightness of the theta direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:39.160
and thus that our rows will have to be bent into&nbsp;
another dimension to be connected. Lastly if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:44.480
consider the second partial derivative of the&nbsp;
Theta component we see that it's a constant which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:50.600
hints to us that we need only one extra dimension&nbsp;
in order to accommodate this bending or curving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.560
and so won't have to worry about&nbsp;
bringing a third dimension into the

00:09:53.560 --> 00:10:01.400
picture. Now from visual intuition alone you've&nbsp;
probably already guessed that we need to bend the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:06.560
rows so that they're touching like this, and&nbsp;
if you're familiar with polar coordinates you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.000
could reasonably surmise that the angle&nbsp;
through which they should be rotated is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:18.840
D-Theta. But how do we extract this information&nbsp;
from the metric tensor? Well to do that we need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:25.720
to invoke something called the Levi-Civita&nbsp;
connection. For infinitesimals like this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:30.200
this connection is expressed as a simple&nbsp;
equality stating that the change in our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:36.280
e-theta basis vector when transported along&nbsp;
the radial direction must equal the change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:43.360
of our ER basis vector when transported in the&nbsp;
theta direction. What does this equality mean

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:50.960
visually? Well consider these two square&nbsp;
infinitesimal pieces of Polar Land side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:55.560
by side. If we transform the theta&nbsp;
lengths of one of the pieces while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.560 --> 00:11:02.280
keeping the other constant we've now added&nbsp;
extra physical space to our manifold. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:06.680
amount of new length is tracked by&nbsp;
noting the change in the E-Theta basis

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:14.080
vector. Now to keep the manifold continuous&nbsp;
there needs to be a change in the radial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.880
basis vector of the next piece atop the&nbsp;
first which will compensate for this new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:25.240
length. Obviously the radial basis vector&nbsp;
just simply growing or shrinking won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.960
compensate for this extra length since&nbsp;
it lies in a wholly different dimension.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:36.800
Thus the radial basis vector must be&nbsp;
rotated in order to supply the additional

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:50.800
length. Now if the theta growth is small,&nbsp;
then this rotation will likewise be small.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:55.200
But if the theta growth is large, then&nbsp;
so too will the required rotation be

00:11:55.200 --> 00:12:05.160
large. So how quickly theta lengths are growing&nbsp;
along the radial direction will in fact determine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:10.360
how rapidly Polar Bear's basis vectors are&nbsp;
rotating when transported along the theta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:18.320
direction. Indeed it is this Levi-Civita condition&nbsp;
that the growing or shrinking of Polar Land along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:23.960
one dimension be compensated by its curving into&nbsp;
another dimension that ultimately causes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:30.360
rotation of Polar Bear's coordinates in the real&nbsp;
world. But what is the amount of this rotation

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:38.520
precisely? Well returning to our infinitesimal&nbsp;
pieces recall that this lower left piece has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:43.760
resized theta length R D-Theta while&nbsp;
the lower right piece has a resized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:50.480
Theta length R plus R D-Theta. The difference&nbsp;
in theta lengths between the lower left and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.480 --> 00:13:02.520
lower right pieces is thus R + DR D-Theta&nbsp;
minus R D-Theta which equals DR * d-Theta.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:08.640
Now the length produced when a radial segment&nbsp;
R is rotated through a small angle D-Theta is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:15.160
R * D-Theta. Here the length of our&nbsp;
radial segment is DR which means to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:23.120
produce the length DR D-Theta it needs&nbsp;
to be rotated through an angle D-Theta.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:27.760
Polar Bear is feeling better about his&nbsp;
reality; the metric tensor gave him the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:33.080
real world lengths of his basis vectors and the&nbsp;
real world value of their adjoining angle, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:40.960
now the Levi-Civita connection gave him the real&nbsp;
world orientation of these basis vectors. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:46.160
armed with such knowledge he now possesses all&nbsp;
the requisite information for how to properly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:53.280
connect his resized infinitesimal pieces of Polar&nbsp;
Land. He simply conjoins the columns in the radial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.280 --> 00:14:01.720
direction side-by-side and then tilts the top row&nbsp;
through an angle D-Theta and voila, he is looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:12.800
no longer at the false geometry of Polar Land but&nbsp;
rather at the true geometry of Cartesian Land.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:17.920
Now it's time for him to formalize this&nbsp;
process by describing precisely how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:21.840
real world vectors corresponding&nbsp;
to his Polar Land basis vectors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:28.160
will change as they are transported&nbsp;
along different coordinate directions.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:32.320
Since he has two basis vectors and there&nbsp;
are two coordinate directions in which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:37.840
these vectors can be transported he will&nbsp;
require four derivative vectors to fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:44.480
describe such change. Each of these derivative&nbsp;
vectors will in turn have two components,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:51.600
meaning eight total numbers will become involved&nbsp;
and it is these eight numbers which are known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:58.680
the Christoffel symbols. The Christoffel&nbsp;
symbols are notated with three indices:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:04.360
the upper index indicates which component&nbsp;
of the derivative vector is being referred

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:14.320
to, the lower left index indicates which&nbsp;
basis vector is having its derivative

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:23.400
taken, and the lower right index indicates in&nbsp;
which coordinate direction we are taking that

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:28.600
derivative.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:35.320
All right, now let's figure out what&nbsp;
these symbols are by calculating each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:40.800
derivative vector. We'll start with the easy one:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:46.600
we'll take the R-basis vector and transport it&nbsp;
a coordinate distance DR in the R direction in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:53.440
Polar Land. Here there is no change in this&nbsp;
basis vector in the real world whatsoever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.440 --> 00:16:00.800
so its derivative vector is zero, meaning our&nbsp;
first two Christoffel symbols are likewise both

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:10.480
zero. Next let's take the theta basis vector and&nbsp;
transport it along a coordinate distance D-Theta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:18.120
in the theta direction in Polar Land. When we do&nbsp;
this, the real world Cartesian vector is rotated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:24.480
counterclockwise through an angle D-Theta. The&nbsp;
change in this vector equals the length produced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:30.520
by this rotation and since the real-world vector&nbsp;
had a length R the length produced by its rotation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:37.360
should equal R D-Theta. Now in this infinitesimal&nbsp;
picture it's easy to see that this rotation occurs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:42.960
relative to the prior piece, but let's take&nbsp;
a moment to look at the continuous picture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:49.480
in Cartesian Land. Here we have the transformed&nbsp;
Theta Vector scaled to its proper length, and as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:56.320
we transport it through a small angle D-Theta&nbsp;
the vector rotates accordingly. But what do we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.320 --> 00:17:03.560
measure its rotation relative to? Well in this&nbsp;
case, we'll transport a second vector alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:09.120
it which maintains a constant orientation in the&nbsp;
direction in which the theta vector was initially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:15.040
pointing before it was transported. Then we&nbsp;
can see that the change in the theta vector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:21.760
is a change relative to this second vector.&nbsp;
This is essentially the same thing we did in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:28.400
the infinitesimal case but in the continuous&nbsp;
case it's referred to as parallel transport.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:37.120
Returning to our calculations, Polar&nbsp;
Bear's theta basis vector thus changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:43.280
by an amount R D-Theta in the real world per&nbsp;
coordinate distance D-Theta in Polar Land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:52.200
so the relevant derivative here is R&nbsp;
D-Theta / D-Theta which equals simply R.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:58.400
The direction this derivative vector is pointing&nbsp;
meanwhile is in the negative radial direction.

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:07.800
Now at different points across Cartesian&nbsp;
Land such a vector will look like this;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:11.520
while at different points across&nbsp;
Polar Land it will look like

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:18.960
this. If we were to express this vector&nbsp;
in its Cartesian basis we would get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:25.000
components minus r cosine of theta in the&nbsp;
X hat direction and minus r sine of theta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:31.040
in the Y hat direction. In Polar Land&nbsp;
however we see that the components of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:35.920
this vector are minus r in the r hat&nbsp;
direction and zero in the theta hat

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:49.120
direction. Our next two Christoffel&nbsp;
components are therefore minus r and zero.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:53.440
Next, let's take the radial basis vector&nbsp;
and transport it a coordinate distance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:59.160
D-Theta in the theta direction in&nbsp;
Polar Land. In Cartesian Land this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:04.640
vector is again subjected to a rotation&nbsp;
D-Theta and since its length is one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:13.920
this rotation produces a length of simply D-Theta.&nbsp;
D-Theta / D-Theta is 1 so the derivative vector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:21.560
everywhere in Cartesian Land has length one&nbsp;
and points in the Theta coordinate direction.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:26.920
However these vectors do not have length&nbsp;
one like this everywhere in Polar Land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:31.760
because if Polar Bear is expressing&nbsp;
them in terms of his basis vectors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:39.720
we must remember that his theta ruler&nbsp;
length is growing across Cartesian Land.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:44.640
At a certain R distance out in polar&nbsp;
land Polar Bear's theta basis vector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:51.360
represents r Cartesian basis vectors, so if&nbsp;
the derivative vector has the length of one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:59.920
Cartesian basis vector it must be shrunk&nbsp;
in Polar Land to a distance of 1 / r. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:05.560
components of the derivative vector are&nbsp;
therefore zero in the r-hat direction and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:17.080
1 divided by r in the theta-hat direction.&nbsp;
These are our next two Christoffel symbols.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:23.200
Last but not least, let's take our theta basis&nbsp;
vector and transport it a length DR in the radial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:32.440
direction in Polar Land. In Cartesian Land the&nbsp;
vector changes by length DR so its derivative is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:43.440
a vector with length DR / DR or 1 which points in&nbsp;
the theta direction. Again normalizing this theta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:49.880
distance in Polar Land we see that our final&nbsp;
two Christoffel components are again 0 and 1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:56.920
/ R. Now of course we could have short-cutted&nbsp;
this process by remembering the Levi-Civita&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.920 --> 00:21:01.600
connection requires that that the derivative of&nbsp;
the theta basis vector when transported in the r&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:14.560
direction equal the derivative of the radial basis&nbsp;
vector when transported in the theta direction.

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:18.800
With all eight Christoffel symbols&nbsp;
calculated Polar Bear now has a much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:25.440
stronger grasp on reality. These symbols&nbsp;
will tell him precisely the rate at which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:30.280
his real-world basis vectors are changing&nbsp;
with respect to changes in his coordinate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:37.440
system. So for instance if he traverses an&nbsp;
infinitesimal length D-Theta in Polar Land&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:41.600
he knows his real world theta basis&nbsp;
vector will shift to the left due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:49.280
picking up a radial component equal to the&nbsp;
Christoffel component there time D-Theta.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.800
If he wants to counter this shift&nbsp;
and continue traveling as straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:58.560
as possible in the real world he will&nbsp;
need to veer rightwards in Polar Land&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:06.160
by an amount which will compensate for&nbsp;
this component, in this case R D-Theta.

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:10.560
Indeed from this knowledge he can begin&nbsp;
constructing something which will prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:21.000
extremely important to him -- his&nbsp;
geodesic paths across Polar Land.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:28.480
Yes, it's a happy ending for Polar Bear who has&nbsp;
finally made his way to the real world. But for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:34.920
us, we have only begun to scratch the surface of&nbsp;
the Christoffel symbols. In ensuing installments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:39.440
we will need to make the relationship between&nbsp;
basis vectors, the Christoffel symbols and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:45.600
the metric tensor explicitly precise; we&nbsp;
will need to begin training for the index

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:53.360
olympics; we will need to move&nbsp;
from flat surfaces to curved ones;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:56.280
and lastly we will need to understand how to swap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:56.280 --> 00:23:03.920
physical manifolds for spacetime manifolds.&nbsp;
But to really truly understand relativity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:11.160
there is only one revelation you need to make. You&nbsp;
are Polar Bear -- you are the one living in The

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:18.240
Matrix. This has been Dialect, thanks for

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:27.880
watching.

